ctors and other individual constituents of an organizational client; the principles governing the representation of organizational clients apply to the representation of governmental organizations."}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/9431132/seiverth-v-perrysburg/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "Seiverth v. Perrysburg", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["2023 Ohio 2319"], "citeCount": 0, "cluster_id": 9431132, "court": "Ohio Court of Claims", "court_citation_string": "Ohio Ct. Cl.", "court_id": "ohioctcl", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2023-06-28", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "2022-00850PQ", "docket_id": 67860471, "judge": "Marti", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2024-06-23T01:14:32.798197Z", "date_created": "2023-10-05T22:22:54.323522Z", "score": {"bm25": 89.78522}}, "neutralCite": "2023 Ohio 2319", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": null, "cites": [2690499, 3698555, 3709692, 3725962, 4413179, 4575031, 4636627, 4636732, 4736563, 6788834, 9439379, 9800999, 9802154], "download_url": "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/13/2023/2023-Ohio-2319.pdf", "id": 9882989, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": "pdf/2023/06/28/seiverth_v._perrysburg.pdf", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-29T04:05:53.586283Z", "date_created": "2023-10-05T22:22:54.332059Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "e3f088f1d837093ba781496bff055ba9ce126e4c", "snippet": "records\n        that were redacted based on <mark>attorney-client privilege</mark> or R.C. 3707.17.\n    -   Respondent be", "type": "combined-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [9882989], "source": "C", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": "Public Records Attorney-Client Privilege R.C. 149.43(A) R.C. 3701.17(B) Public Office's burden of proving the applicability of an exemption from the general duty to provide access to records Burden of proving the elements of attorney-client privilege Failure to explain bases for redactions based on attorney-client privilege precludes the privilege Disclosure of privileged records to adverse party waives attorney-client privilege. R.C. 3701.17(B) does not justify withholding of records absent proof that the information in the records was reported to or obtained by one of the health-related entities listed in the statute."}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/9497197/schafer-v-levey/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "Schafer v. Levey", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["2024 Ohio 1605"], "citeCount": 0, "cluster_id": 9497197, "court": "Ohio Court of Appeals", "court_citation_string": "Ohio Ct. App.", "court_id": "ohioctapp", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2024-04-26", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "C-230410", "docket_id": 68474953, "judge": "Kinsley", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2024-06-23T01:30:40.746513Z", "date_created": "2024-04-26T13:09:16.625367Z", "score": {"bm25": 89.68042}}, "neutralCite": "2024 Ohio 1605", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": null, "cites": [2692016, 3699614, 4105166, 7801771], "download_url": "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/1/2024/2024-Ohio-1605.pdf", "id": 9963810, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": "pdf/2024/04/26/schafer_v._levey.pdf", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-07-09T05:08:27.348249Z", "date_created": "2024-04-26T13:09:16.637665Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "60b01187ecbb476c82ad46dd18bf4ed11e14569c", "snippet": "determining any reason for invading the <mark>attorney-client\n\nprivilege</mark>, the trial court required Schafer to", "type": "combined-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [9963810], "source": "C", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": "JURISDICTION \u2014ATTORNEY-CLIENT PRIVILEGE \u2014 DISCOVERY: The trial court erred in granting defendant's motion to compel communications between plaintiff and her former attorney without conducting an evidentiary hearing or in-camera review to determine the applicability of the attorney-client privilege."}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/10006764/12312-mayfield-rd-llc-v-high-low-little-italy-llc/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "12312 Mayfield Rd., L.L.C. v. High & Low Little Italy, L.L.C.", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["247 N.E.3d 1135", "2024 Ohio 2717"], "citeCount": 9, "cluster_id": 10006764, "court": "Ohio Court of Appeals", "court_citation_string": "Ohio Ct. App.", "court_id": "ohioctapp", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2024-07-18", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "113549", "docket_id": 68955210, "judge": "Kilbane", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-26T17:55:00.352063Z", "date_created": "2024-07-18T16:14:15.217998Z", "score": {"bm25": 85.89987}}, "neutralCite": "2024 Ohio 2717", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": 8109, "cites": [111419, 255675, 557229, 2691457, 2692055, 2755801, 3696381, 3765666, 3782990, 4121339, 5116802, 6758010, 6758110, 6759975, 6760133, 8374919, 8621665, 9038341, 9926726], "download_url": "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/8/2024/2024-Ohio-2717.pdf", "id": 10473365, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": "pdf/2024/07/18/12312_mayfield_rd._l.l.c._v._high__low_little_italy_l.l.c..pdf", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-26T17:55:00.342119Z", "date_created": "2024-07-18T16:14:15.233520Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "b17671b6394696652a6752a19ef7090228d1dd5c", "snippet": "Mayfield claims are protected by the <mark>attorney-client privilege</mark>. For the reasons that\n\nfollow, we reverse", "type": "combined-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [10473365], "source": "C", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": "Motion to compel attorney-client privilege R.C. 2317.02 discovery request agency in camera inspection evidentiary hearing. The trial court abused its discretion when it granted defendant-appellee's motion to compel without first conducting an evidentiary hearing or in camera inspection of the documents to determine whether plaintiff-appellant's real estate agents/brokers were agents for attorney-client privilege purposes."}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/9471476/fiani-v-worldpay-llc/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "Fiani v. Worldpay, L.L.C.", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["234 N.E.3d 1235", "2024 Ohio 304"], "citeCount": 2, "cluster_id": 9471476, "court": "Ohio Court of Appeals", "court_citation_string": "Ohio Ct. App.", "court_id": "ohioctapp", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2024-01-31", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "C-230175", "docket_id": 68218404, "judge": "Crouse", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-26T17:48:47.924821Z", "date_created": "2024-02-02T14:07:20.344985Z", "score": {"bm25": 84.68145}}, "neutralCite": "2024 Ohio 304", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": null, "cites": [201815, 3713141, 3726049, 3754191, 4583629, 6330706, 6336941, 6755085, 6762597, 6763472, 6776714, 9381972, 9481369, 9801851, 9802115, 11151143], "download_url": "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/1/2024/2024-Ohio-304.pdf", "id": 9929314, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": "pdf/2024/01/31/fiani_v._worldpay_l.l.c..pdf", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-29T09:42:39.006417Z", "date_created": "2024-02-02T14:07:20.382033Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "216b248d3dc2bfc304360b4f45e5ceecdf657e00", "snippet": "untimely and selective waiver of the <mark>attorney-client privilege</mark>. Finding Fiani\u2019s\n\narguments to be without", "type": "combined-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [9929314], "source": "C", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": "CIV.R. 15 \u2013 MOTION FOR LEAVE TO AMEND COMPLAINT \u2013 ATTORNEY-CLIENT PRIVILEGE \u2013 WAIVER: The trial court did not abuse its discretion in denying plaintiff's motion for leave to amend the complaint where the amendment was not timely and would have been futile. Where defendants informed plaintiff that they intended to waive the attorney-client privilege, despite asserting it in discovery, three months before the trial was scheduled and six months before the trial actually took place, defendants offered to reopen depositions at their expense, and plaintiff did not file a motion in limine regarding the waiver and admission of related evidence at trial, the trial court did not abuse its discretion in overruling plaintiff's objection to defendants' waiver of the attorney-client privilege."}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/10622879/dye-v-cleveland/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "Dye v. Cleveland", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["2025 Ohio 2375"], "citeCount": 2, "cluster_id": 10622879, "court": "Ohio Court of Claims", "court_citation_string": "Ohio Ct. Cl.", "court_id": "ohioctcl", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2025-06-03", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "2025-00216PQ", "docket_id": 70702012, "judge": "Marti", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-07-03T18:11:05.827362Z", "date_created": "2025-07-03T18:11:05.756798Z", "score": {"bm25": 83.39275}}, "neutralCite": "2025 Ohio 2375", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": null, "cites": [2690162, 2690499, 2690691, 2691133, 3695380, 3742440, 4112494, 4177093, 4184658, 4297140, 4341483, 4341484, 4384063, 4392057, 4395945, 4413179, 4502906, 4575031, 4577280, 4636627, 4636732, 4911972, 7089206, 7798826, 8212307, 9386336, 9399586, 9801131, 9801851, 9802171, 9879544, 9882997, 9915233, 9940921, 10034193, 10453264, 10466259, 10784694, 10799373], "download_url": "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/13/2025/2025-Ohio-2375.pdf", "id": 11089467, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": "pdf/2025/06/03/dye_v._cleveland.pdf", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-01T18:00:46.359449Z", "date_created": "2025-07-03T18:11:05.770162Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "969006eec89d07e20b324e5f03faf20071a1252d", "snippet": "specifically challenged were based on the\n<mark>attorney-client privilege</mark>, and none of the redactions to records", "type": "combined-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [11089467], "source": "C", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": "Public Records; R.C. 149.43(A); R.C. 149.43(A)(1)(g) and (4); R.C. 2743.75; R.C. 2743.75(E)(3)(c); Attorney-Client Privilege; A court should be hesitant to dispose of potentially meritorious claims based on a lay person's inartful submissions in a case brought pursuant to R.C. 2743.75 because that statute is intended to provide a forum for those that are not schooled in the law; Evidence filed after deadlines set pursuant to R.C. 2743.75(E)(3)(c) should not be considered over the opposing party's objection; A court will only undertake individualized scrutiny of redactions if they are specifically challenged; The work product doctrine is distinct from the attorney-client privilege and fits within a different exemption from the Public Records Act; Communications about public relations concerns are not protected by the attorney-client privilege absent evidence that the public relations communications involved the formulation of legal, rather than public relations, advice; R.C. 149.43 does not require public offices to provide privilege logs."}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/9501635/rehm-v-eckinger/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "Rehm v. Eckinger", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["242 N.E.3d 222", "2024 Ohio 1860"], "citeCount": 0, "cluster_id": 9501635, "court": "Ohio Court of Appeals", "court_citation_string": "Ohio Ct. App.", "court_id": "ohioctapp", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2024-05-10", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "2023CA00113", "docket_id": 68524554, "judge": "Delaney", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-26T18:21:37.397727Z", "date_created": "2024-05-13T21:06:33.281692Z", "score": {"bm25": 82.723885}}, "neutralCite": "2024 Ohio 1860", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": 8076, "cites": [110374, 118237, 2691457, 3160327, 3205789, 3767454, 4105164, 4582855, 4728145, 6667759, 6787782, 9324559, 9882795], "download_url": "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/5/2024/2024-Ohio-1860.pdf", "id": 9968248, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": "pdf/2024/05/10/rehm_v._eckinger.pdf", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-26T18:21:37.355235Z", "date_created": "2024-05-13T21:06:33.319989Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "d506018e0784da30a10fb9084f973bfe33837f37", "snippet": "Appellant as Executor\n\n would not waive <mark>attorney-client privilege</mark> between Attorney Craemer Smith and the", "type": "combined-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [9968248], "source": "C", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": "attorney-client privilege, self-protection exception"}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/10633447/barrett-v-wagenbrenner/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "Barrett v. Wagenbrenner", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["2025 Ohio 2494"], "citeCount": 0, "cluster_id": 10633447, "court": "Ohio Court of Appeals", "court_citation_string": "Ohio Ct. App.", "court_id": "ohioctapp", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2025-07-15", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "24AP-555", "docket_id": 70804024, "judge": "Dingus, J.", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-07-15T21:12:31.993556Z", "date_created": "2025-07-15T19:11:24.437904Z", "score": {"bm25": 81.02612}}, "neutralCite": "2025 Ohio 2494", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": null, "cites": [92351, 2702507, 3693458, 3732514, 3753720, 3781087, 4105166, 4424781, 6658892, 6672949, 6674187, 6752381, 6759975, 6776595, 8789035, 8795493, 9040143, 9322853, 9426145, 9428127, 9802147], "download_url": "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/10/2025/2025-Ohio-2494.pdf", "id": 11100034, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": "pdf/2025/07/15/barrett_v._wagenbrenner.pdf", "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-01T19:27:21.219104Z", "date_created": "2025-07-15T19:11:24.450580Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "2599c8551e101d2dbb7141a5055c679649c81558", "snippet": "that the Wagenbrenners had\nwaived their <mark>attorney-client privilege</mark> with Thomas Geyer (\u201cAttorney Geyer\u201d) related", "type": "combined-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [11100034], "source": "C", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": "On interlocutory appeal. The trial court erred in holding that the defendants had waived their attorney-client privilege. Consenting to an attorney's appearance as a testifying witness is not enough, by itself, to constitute an express waiver of the privilege under R.C. 2317.02(A)(1). An attorney's testimony about non-privileged information does not implicate R.C. 2317.02(A)(1). Because the statute does not provide for implied waivers of the attorney-client privilege, Ohio courts cannot apply the common-law rule of implied waiver. Judgment reversed."}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/10609988/whitney-v-jm-smucker-co/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "Whitney v. J.M. Smucker Co.", "caseNameFull": "", "citation": ["2025 Ohio 2141"], "citeCount": 1, "c